/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A table made in the rabbit is handed to a function beside an outer series, then a rabbit's series is stored into its first element.

    A name records where the NAME was made; the store is judged against where what it reaches
    was made, which can be further out. Judged once everything is checked, so a later statement
    that lowers it counts too (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Bind void to put, given (the series of series of series of number holder, the series of series of number rows):
    Insert rows into holder.
Done.
Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define holder as a series of series of series of number.
    Cast put on (holder, keeper).
    Insert (a series of number with (1)) into item 1 of holder.
Done.
State keeper.
